<div class="mt-12 bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-sm">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">About These Calculators &amp; Official Sources</h2>
  
  <p class="text-gray-700 text-base mb-6">
    Every calculator on CalcForDIY runs entirely in your browser—no account needed, no data uploaded to a server, and instant results. To ensure maximum accuracy, all mathematical models and material waste factors are built using official primary sources and recognized trade standards.
  </p>

  <h3 class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-900 mb-4 bg-blue-50 py-1.5 px-3 rounded-md inline-block">
    Verified Formulas &amp; Industry Standards
  </h3>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-6 text-sm text-gray-700">
    <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-100 rounded-lg p-4">
      <div class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-blue-600">📐</span> Tile, Grout &amp; Thinset
      </div>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-xs leading-relaxed">
        Formulas derived from the <strong>Tile Council of North America (TCNA) Handbook</strong>, combined with technical coverage data sheets from leading manufacturers <strong>Mapei</strong> and <strong>LATICRETE</strong>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-100 rounded-lg p-4">
      <div class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-blue-600">🪵</span> Flooring &amp; Subfloor
      </div>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-xs leading-relaxed">
        Waste factors and box coverage calculations follow guidelines from the <strong>National Wood Flooring Association (NWFA)</strong> and <strong>APA – The Engineered Wood Association</strong>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-100 rounded-lg p-4">
      <div class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-blue-600">🧱</span> Concrete &amp; Rebar
      </div>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-xs leading-relaxed">
        Cubic volume equations and bag yield rates follow <strong>Quikrete &amp; Sakrete</strong> manufacturer specifications and <strong>American Concrete Institute (ACI 318)</strong> reinforcement standards.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-100 rounded-lg p-4">
      <div class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-blue-600">🔨</span> Framing, Drywall &amp; Walls
      </div>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-xs leading-relaxed">
        Stud spacing, corner backing, and plate calculations follow the <strong>International Residential Code (IRC)</strong> and <strong>Gypsum Association (GA-216)</strong> drywall installation standards.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-100 rounded-lg p-4">
      <div class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-blue-600">💡</span> Lighting &amp; Electrical Safety
      </div>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-xs leading-relaxed">
        Foot-candle targets are sourced from the <strong>Illuminating Engineering Society (IES)</strong>. Circuit loads, wattage limits, and cord safety follow <strong>National Electrical Code (NEC Article 210)</strong> 80% continuous load rules.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-100 rounded-lg p-4">
      <div class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-blue-600">⚡</span> Energy Costs &amp; HVAC
      </div>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-xs leading-relaxed">
        Utility calculations use benchmarks from the <strong>U.S. Energy Information Administration (EIA)</strong> and performance rating standards from <strong>AHRI</strong> (Air-Conditioning, Heating, and Refrigeration Institute).
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 border-t border-gray-100 pt-4">
    Whether you are a first-time DIYer planning a weekend project or a contractor running quick job site estimates, CalcForDIY is designed to deliver fast, transparent, and mathematically sound calculations every time.
  </p>
</div>
